Find the midpoint $M$ of the interval joining $A(-1, 5)$ and $B(3, -1)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.55]
\draw[step=1,gray!25,very thin] (-5,-5) grid (5,5);
\draw[<->] (-5.5,0)--(5.5,0) node[right]{$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-5.5)--(0,5.5) node[above]{$y$};
\foreach \i in {-5,-4,-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4,5} \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\i,0){$\i$};
\foreach \i in {-5,-4,-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4,5} \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,\i){$\i$};
\draw[thick,blue] (-1,5)--(3,-1);
\fill (-1,5) circle (2.5pt);
\node[above left,fill=white,inner sep=1pt,font=\scriptsize] at (-1,5){$A(-1,5)$};
\fill (3,-1) circle (2.5pt);
\node[below right,fill=white,inner sep=1pt,font=\scriptsize] at (3,-1){$B(3,-1)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

